SEC. 51P-1118.119. RETIREMENT HOUSING RESTRICTIVE COVENANT.

(a) In general. In order to receive the retirement housing density bonus in Section 51P- 1118.111, a retirement housing restrictive covenant must be executed and recorded in accordance with this section on a form provided by the city. The instrument must:

(1) be signed by all owners of the Property;

(2) be signed by all lienholders, other than taxing entities, having an interest in the Property;

(3) contain a legal description of the Property;

(4) specify that 116 retirement housing dwelling units or suites must be provided;

(5) be a covenant running with the land;

(6) be for a term of 20 years;

(7) state that all signatories agree to defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the City of Dallas from and against all claims or liabilities arising out of or in connection with the instrument;

(8) state that it may only be amended or terminated by a subsequent written instrument that is:

(A) signed by all owners of the Property and all lienholders, other than taxing entities;

(B) approved by the director;

(C) approved as to form by the city attorney; and

(D) recorded and made a part of the deed records of the county or counties in which the Property is located;

(9) state that the owner agrees to maintain the property in compliance with all federal, state, and local health and safety regulations;

(10) state that the owner agrees to notify the city within 30 days of any change in ownership, default, foreclosure, or bankruptcy;

(11) state that it may be enforced by the City of Dallas;

(12) state that it shall be governed by the laws of the State of Texas; and

(13) be approved by the director and be approved as to form by city attorney.

(b) Instrument to be recorded. A true and correct copy of the fully executed retirement housing restrictive covenant must be recorded in the deed records of the county or counties in which the property is located. The instrument will not be considered effective until it is recorded in the deed records in accordance with this article and a recorded copy of the instrument is filed with the director.

(c) Expiration. Upon termination of the retirement housing period and expiration of the retirement housing restrictive covenant, the retirement housing density bonus in Section 51P- 1118.111(d)(3) may remain on the Property. (Ord. 33054)

SEC. 51A-1118.120. TRANSIT RIDERSHIP ENHANCEMENTS.

(a) In general. This district is intended to enhance public transportation ridership by providing the enhancements in this section.

(b) Covered transit shelter. A minimum of two covered transit shelter stations with seating must be provided to serve the existing Dallas Area Rapid Transit (DART) bus stop to encourage additional transit ridership. One covered transit shelter station must be located on Preston Road and one covered transit shelter station must be located on Belt Line Road in conjunction with the applicable development phase. Direct pedestrian connections between the DART bus stop and all buildings must be provided. (Ord. 33054)
